[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Barmen Defense"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "d4-pawn-centre,tempo-gain,development-lead"]
[Kind "main"]

1. e4 c5
2. c3
2... d5
3. exd5 { Wins a pawn for the moment and opens the e-file. Black has to recapture, and either way a Black piece comes out early. }
3... Qxd5
(3... Nf6 4. Bb5+ { Check first, so Black must spend a move answering it before taking back on d5. } 4... Bd7 5. Bc4 b5 6. Be2 Nxd5 7. Nf3)
(3... Nf6 4. Bb5+ Nbd7 5. Nf3 Nxd5 6. d4)
4. d4 { Takes the centre. Nc3 cannot hit the queen the way it does against the Scandinavian, because the c3 pawn is in the way, so White develops and plays d4 first. }
4... Nf6
5. Nf3 { Guards d4 and blocks the queen's diagonal to g2, the pawn White cannot easily defend yet. [%cal Gf3d4] }
5... e6
(5... Nc6 6. Be3 e6 7. Na3)
6. Bd3 { Develops the bishop to a good diagonal and clears f1 so White can castle. }
6... Be7
7. O-O O-O
8. Qe2 { Plan: Rd1 and Na3 or Nbd2, and if Black takes on d4, recapture with the c-pawn and play Nc3 with tempo, hitting the queen. If Black leaves the book, develop everything and keep d4 guarded. } *
